WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
If you have tried direct pressure and wound packing, but the bleeding on an arm or leg just won't stop, it is potentially life-threatening situation.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.000
In this case, for anyone age 2 and older, we need to move quickly to apply a tourniquet.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
For children under the age of 2, remember to continue using direct pressure instead.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Your instructor will demonstrate and pass out tourniquets so you can practice together.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:34.000
To apply a tourniquet, first place the tourniquet 2 to 3 inches above the wound, making sure you aren't placing it directly over a joint like an elbow or knee.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Pull the strap as tight as you possibly can and secure it.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Then, you'll turn the windlass, that's the stick-like rod on the device, until the bleeding completely stops.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Once it's secure, your final step is to record the exact time you put it on.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
This is vital information for the surgeons who will treat the person later.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Most importantly, once that tourniquet is on, do not take it off for any reason.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Only a doctor in a hospital should do that.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
For our practice today, I want you to apply the tourniquet to your own arm or leg.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.000
You don't need to tighten it to the point of stopping blood flow, but I want you to tighten the strap until you feel firm pressure,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.000
and then give the windlass a few turns until you feel that pressure increase.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Once you've felt how the mechanism works, you can take it off and go ahead and dispose of your used gauze squares and rolls.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Finally, removing your gloves in the proper manner helps to keep ourselves safe from contamination.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Using your dominant hand, pinch the outside of the opposite glove near the wrist, being careful not to touch your skin,

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.000
and peel it downward so it turns inside out as it comes off.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Hold that crumpled glove in your still-gloved hand.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Now, slide the fingers of your clean hand under the wrist cuff of the remaining glove and peel it off over the first one.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.000
This should leave both gloves inside out and nested together.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Drop them straight into the biohazard container and immediately wash your hands with soap and water for at least 30 seconds.

